    "pdfPageEnd": 94
  },
  "rulesText": "A pool is a collection of tokens shared by multiple adversaries. Each pool has a unique name, which is typically the name shared by the adversaries it affects. Unlike standard adversary tokens, pool tokens are not placed on a stat block; instead, the GM collects them in a separate location. Pools are empty when the scene begins and cleared when the scene ends.",
